From 1d16e381c351057c6c94147a75a0133df5f8b7c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alaric McKenzie-Boone <alaric.mckenzie.boone@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:20:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Drive the Bulbmin bridge from the Chappy-family registration
 (#131)

Lane 11 turned the inert Bulbmin ledger into an opt-in driver:

* pc_p2_bulbmin_drive_birth() / attach_mother() run the source
  LeafChappy::birthChildren() ten-dependent loop through pikiMgr->birth()
  and the existing Kochappy registration, which is the mother stand-in.
* The real Navi::callPikis whistle path recruits wild dependents in place
  and claims the bound lane-12 captain ownership table (slot 0).
* Death/reuse hooks: pc_p2_bulbmin_leader_died()/proxy_forget() release
  only wild dependents from the forgotten Chappy actor; PikiMgr::birth()
  forgets a recycled slot's stale dependent id.
* Engine-free P2BulbminDriver mirrors the loop; the bridge test proves ten
  capped dependents, whistle recruitment, leader-death release and the cave
  descend/exit filter.

Inert without PIKMIN_P2_BULBMIN/p2-bulbmin.txt; no live LeafChappy actor is
claimed (missing piki_kochappy model).
